The test file can't be `tsc`-checked in this bare repo because there is no `bun:test` type declaration available, but it runs under the project's own `bun test` check. There are no other scripts in `package.json` (only `test`).

## Decisions the plan didn't specify

- **`set` on an existing key does not count as a use.** The spec explicitly says only a successful `get` counts as a use, and says `set` replaces value/time "without evicting anything", so I update the entry in place (keeping its LRU position) rather than moving it to MRU.
- **Expired entries are physically purged** in `set` and `size` so they can never cause a live entry to be evicted; they are also removed when touched by `get`/`has`/`delete`.
- **Expiry boundary:** an entry is expired once `now() >= setTime + ttlMs` (at exactly `ttlMs` it is expired).

